 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Compare Simple Forecast Models\n",
    "This notebook evaluates two simple forecasting models: a 3-point moving average and a naive last-value forecast.\n",
    "It uses a synthetic sine wave time series with added noise as input data.\n",
    "The primary metrics for evaluation are Mean Squared Error (MSE) and Mean Absolute Error (MAE), quantifying predictive accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "The evaluation workflow includes:\n",
    "1. Generating synthetic time series data.\n",
    "2. Calculating predictions for both the 3-point moving average and naive last-value models.\n",
    "3. Computing MSE and MAE for each model.\n",
    "4. Presenting aggregate metrics and detailed per-example results, including true values, predictions, and errors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup\n",
    "### Install Dependencies\n",
    "This cell installs all necessary Python packages. It uses a conditional installation to ensure compatibility with both Google Colab and local environments. In Colab, pre-installed packages like `numpy` and `pandas` are often at specific versions, so we avoid reinstalling them. For other environments, all packages are installed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "install_deps",
    "outputId": "c04481b7-a367-4286-9a2f-e8b940984852"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "def install_and_import(package, import_name=None):\n",
    "    if import_name is None: \n",
    "        import_name = package\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        __import__(import_name)\n",
    "        print(\"{} is already installed.\".format(package))\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        print(\"Installing {}...\".format(package))\n",
    "        subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", package])\n",
    "        print(\"{} installed successfully.\".format(package))\n",
    "\n",
    "# List of packages to install\n",
    "packages = [\n",
    "    (\"loguru\", \"loguru\"),\n",
    "    (\"numpy\", \"numpy\"),\n",
    "    (\"scikit-learn\", \"sklearn\"), # scikit-learn for sklearn.metrics\n",
    "    (\"matplotlib\", \"matplotlib\") # For plotting\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "for package, import_name in packages:\n",
    "    install_and_import(package, import_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"All packages checked and installed if necessary.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Imports\n",
    "Import all necessary libraries, including `loguru` for logging, `numpy` for numerical operations, `sklearn.metrics` for evaluation, and `matplotlib` for visualization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from loguru import logger\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_error\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Configure loguru to output to stdout, disable file logging for notebook simplicity\n",
    "logger.remove()\n",
    "logger.add(sys.stdout, level=\"INFO\", format=\"{time:HH:mm:ss}|{level:<7}|{message}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data Loading Helper\n",
    "This helper function loads the `mini_demo_data.json` file. It first attempts to load from a GitHub URL for Colab compatibility and then falls back to a local file if the URL fails or is not accessible."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "GITHUB_DATA_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AMGrobelnik/ai-invention-1560d8-micro-niche-adaptive-forecasting-for-sho/main/round-1/evaluation-1/demo/mini_demo_data.json\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_data():\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        import urllib.request\n",
    "        with urllib.request.urlopen(GITHUB_DATA_URL) as response:\n",
    "            return json.loads(response.read().decode())\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        logger.warning(\"Could not load data from GitHub URL: {}. Falling back to local file.\".format(e))\n",
    "    if Path(\"mini_demo_data.json\").exists():\n",
    "        with open(\"mini_demo_data.json\", 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Could not load mini_demo_data.json from GitHub or local path.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Load Data\n",
    "Load the curated `mini_demo_data.json` which contains a small synthetic time series dataset for demonstration purposes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "demo_data = load_data()\n",
    "logger.info(\"Demo data loaded successfully.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration\n",
    "Define tunable parameters for generating the synthetic time series. These values are set to minimal levels for a quick demonstration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Tunable parameters\n",
    "SERIES_LENGTH = 20  # Number of points in the synthetic time series (original: 20)\n",
    "NOISE_STD_DEV = 0.1 # Standard deviation of the noise added to the sine wave (original: 0.1)\n",
    "RANDOM_SEED = 42    # Random seed for reproducibility"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Processing\n",
    "### Generate Synthetic Time Series Data\n",
    "A synthetic sine wave time series with added Gaussian noise is generated to simulate input data for the forecasting models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "np.random.seed(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
    "true_values = np.sin(np.linspace(0, 3 * np.pi, SERIES_LENGTH)) + np.random.normal(0, NOISE_STD_DEV, SERIES_LENGTH)\n",
    "logger.info(\"Generated synthetic time series of length {}.\".format(SERIES_LENGTH))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Generate Predictions: 3-point Moving Average\n",
    "This section implements a 3-point moving average forecasting model. For each point, the prediction is the average of the three preceding true values. Edge cases for the first few points are handled separately."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "moving_avg_predictions = []\n",
    "moving_avg_predictions.append(true_values[0]) # For the first point, no prior data. Use the true value itself\n",
    "if SERIES_LENGTH > 1:\n",
    "    moving_avg_predictions.append(true_values[0]) # For the second point, only one prior data point. Use the first true value.\n",
    "if SERIES_LENGTH > 2:\n",
    "    moving_avg_predictions.append(np.mean(true_values[0:2])) # For the third point, two prior data points. Average them.\n",
    "\n",
    "# For subsequent points, use a 3-point moving average of *past* values\n",
    "for i in range(3, SERIES_LENGTH):\n",
    "    moving_avg_predictions.append(np.mean(true_values[i-3:i]))\n",
    "\n",
    "moving_avg_predictions = np.array(moving_avg_predictions)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure predictions array is the same length as true_values.\n",
    "# If series_length < 3, this padding logic ensures correct length.\n",
    "while len(moving_avg_predictions) < SERIES_LENGTH:\n",
    "    moving_avg_predictions = np.append(moving_avg_predictions, moving_avg_predictions[-1]) # Pad with last valid prediction\n",
    "moving_avg_predictions = moving_avg_predictions[:SERIES_LENGTH]\n",
    "\n",
    "logger.info(\"Generated 3-point moving average predictions.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Generate Predictions: Naive Last-Value Forecast\n",
    "This section implements a naive forecasting model, where the prediction for the current step is simply the value from the immediately preceding step. For the very first point, it uses its own true value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "naive_predictions = [true_values[max(0, i-1)] for i in range(SERIES_LENGTH)]\n",
    "naive_predictions = np.array(naive_predictions)\n",
    "logger.info(\"Generated naive last-value forecast predictions.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Calculate Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "Mean Squared Error (MSE) and Mean Absolute Error (MAE) are calculated for both forecasting models by comparing their predictions against the true values of the synthetic time series."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "metrics = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3-point moving average\n",
    "mse_ma = mean_squared_error(true_values, moving_avg_predictions)\n",
    "mae_ma = mean_absolute_error(true_values, moving_avg_predictions)\n",
    "metrics[\"moving_average\"] = {\"MSE\": mse_ma, \"MAE\": mae_ma}\n",
    "logger.info(\"Moving Average - MSE: {:.4f}, MAE: {:.4f}\".format(mse_ma, mae_ma))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Naive last-value forecast\n",
    "mse_naive = mean_squared_error(true_values, naive_predictions)\n",
    "mae_naive = mean_absolute_error(true_values, naive_predictions)\n",
    "metrics[\"naive_forecast\"] = {\"MSE\": mse_naive, \"MAE\": mae_naive}\n",
    "logger.info(\"Naive Forecast - MSE: {:.4f}, MAE: {:.4f}\".format(mse_naive, mae_naive))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Results\n",
    "### Summary and Visualization\n",
    "This section presents the aggregated evaluation metrics and visualizes the true values alongside the predictions from both models. The visualization helps in understanding the performance and behavior of each forecasting approach on the synthetic time series."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"\\n--- Aggregate Metrics ---\")\n",
    "for model, model_metrics in metrics.items():\n",
    "    print(\"{}.replace('_\', ' ').title() - MSE: {:.4f}, MAE: {:.4f}\".format(model, model_metrics[\'MSE\'], model_metrics[\'MAE\']))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plotting the results\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "plt.plot(true_values, label='True Values', marker='o', linestyle='-', color='blue')\n",
    "plt.plot(moving_avg_predictions, label='3-Point Moving Average Predictions', marker='x', linestyle='--', color='red')\n",
    "plt.plot(naive_predictions, label='Naive Last-Value Forecast Predictions', marker='^', linestyle=':', color='green')\n",
    "plt.title('Synthetic Time Series Forecasting Comparison')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Time Step')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Value')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Per-Example Details from Demo Data ---\")\n",
    "if demo_data and demo_data[\'datasets\'] and demo_data[\'datasets\'][0][\'examples\']:\n",
    "    for i, example in enumerate(demo_data[\'datasets\'][0][\'examples\']):\n",
    "        print(\"\\nTime Step {}:\".format(i))\n",
    "        print(\"  True Value: {:.4f}\".format(float(example[\'output\'])))\n",
    "        print(\"  Moving Avg Pred: {:.4f} (SE: {:.4f}, AE: {:.4f})\".format(float(example[\'predict_moving_average\']), example[\'eval_squared_error_ma\'], example[\'eval_absolute_error_ma\']))\n",
    "        print(\"  Naive Pred: {:.4f} (SE: {:.4f}, AE: {:.4f})\".format(float(example[\'predict_naive_forecast\']), example[\'eval_squared_error_naive\'], example[\'eval_absolute_error_naive\']))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"No example details found in demo data.\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
